      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Camden’s historic depot, built in 1900, sits on land once owned by Jonathan Martin, an early town landowner.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofcamden.org/camden-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Camden Masonic Temple, the 1952 high school gymnasium, and the Andrew Thomas House are all listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camden%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The local history book “Camden II” was assembled from photos and newspaper stories collected through a Facebook page, the first local history to use social media.",
